== Officially mentioned ==

These are features that have been talked about or shared publicly by VRChat staff. They may be in development, but they do not yet have an Open Beta testing branch or a confirmed live release.

=== New character controller for worlds ===

A long-running request proposes a replacement world character controller with better moving platform support, smoother stairs and slopes, improved unstuck behavior, collider push interaction, and broader Udon control.<ref name="CannyNewCharacterController">[https://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/new-character-controller-for-worlds "New Character Controller for Worlds"] on ''feedback.vrchat.com''; posted April 30, 2024; retrieved March 14, 2026.</ref>

The thread is currently marked ''interested''. A staff update on the post says work is currently halted while other projects are prioritized, with a note that updates will be shared if the item re-enters the roadmap.<ref name="CannyNewCharacterController" />

In April 2026, VRChat employee Sai confirmed on X that the new character controller remains "on the back burner" with no ETA and is not currently being worked on.<ref name="SaiXPost">[https://x.com/Sairenix/status/2042786856899629187 Post] on ''x.com''; posted April 11, 2026; retrieved April 12, 2026.</ref>

=== Avatar preview improvements ===

A request proposes raising the camera used in avatar previews, instead of the current bottom-up view focused on the lower half of the body.<ref name="Canny1642AvatarPreview">[https://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-marketplace/p/1642-camera-angle-avatar-preview "[1642] Camera Angle Avatar Preview"] on ''feedback.vrchat.com''; posted May 22, 2025; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref>

The thread is currently marked ''interested''. A staff update on {{Date|2025-05-23}} said improving avatar previews in general was part of planning for the second half of 2025, with no promises.<ref name="Canny1642AvatarPreview" />

=== Age assurance rollout ===

The next Age Assurance phase beyond [[VRC+]] is planned for the United Kingdom and has not been announced as started. [[Age Assurance]] through [[VRC+]] remains the current live method.

In December 2025, VRChat stated it is working to reduce the cost of age verification through negotiation, partnership, and optimization, without announcing a price point. The long-term goal is to make verification free for everyone if finances permit.<ref name="TrustSafety2025Blog">[https://hello.vrchat.com/blog/trust-safety-update-2025 "Safety, Freedom, and the Future of VRChat"] on ''hello.vrchat.com''; dated December 19, 2025; retrieved June 9, 2026.</ref> The same announcement expected [[Age Verification]] to function alongside reintroduced [[Content Gating]] in the first half of 2026.

In a June 2026 update, VRChat adopted the term "age assurance" as an umbrella covering both age verification and age estimation, and said it would lean more on estimation approaches going forward.<ref name="SafetyUpdate2026">[https://hello.vrchat.com/blog/june-2026-safety-update "Update: Age Assurance, Content Gating, and Safety Improvements in VRChat"] on ''hello.vrchat.com''; dated June 24, 2026; retrieved June 25, 2026.</ref> VRChat stated that "once we start doing this, you'll get a link to go get age-assured." The UK rollout is planned in waves over several months and would be offered free of charge during an initial period. [[VRC+]] subscribers would keep immediate access. VRChat gave no date for a wider rollout beyond the United Kingdom, citing cost and coverage challenges.<ref name="SafetyUpdate2026" />

=== Content gating reintroduction ===

User-toggleable [[Content Gating]] filters are already live. Age-based forced gating has not begun.

VRChat announced it will reintroduce age-based forced gating so that some tagged content requires [[Age Verification]] to view.<ref name="TrustSafety2025Blog" /> At the time, the change was expected in the first half of 2026.

The stated goal is a baseline expectation of content safety for public instances. Public instances and non-verified spaces must be suitable for a general audience. The system is meant to set a standard for what content is permissible where, and to reduce exposure to adult or suggestive content in broadly accessible spaces.<ref name="TrustSafety2025Blog" />

The upcoming change is age-based forced gating of "Sexually Suggestive" content in the United Kingdom. It is planned to follow the United Kingdom age assurance rollout by a few months and has not begun. Users who are not age assured, or whose age is determined to be under 18, would have the "Sexually Suggestive" filter turned on with no option to disable it. Affected content would be hidden behind a placeholder. This is the only filter category changing at that time. VRChat said it could extend gating more broadly later, and advised creators to tag affected content ahead of a grace period before enforcement.<ref name="SafetyUpdate2026" />

=== Group moderation tools ===

VRChat stated it is exploring ways to give [[Groups|group]] owners and moderators stronger tools to enforce community norms and take consistent action against bad actors.<ref name="TrustSafety2025Blog" /> No specific tools or timeline were announced.

=== Age assured groups ===

In a June 2026 update, VRChat stated it intends to build [[Groups]] that require members to be age assured as 18 or older to join. It described this as a feature planned for after the underlying age assurance systems are established, and framed it as a preview that is subject to change.<ref name="SafetyUpdate2026" />

=== Public instance behavior system ===

VRChat stated it is experimenting with a system aimed at reducing toxicity and bad behavior in public instances, which it described as one of the longest-running complaints about the platform. It framed this as part of a broader Trust & Safety effort that also includes growing investment, reducing the time between a report being filed and action being taken, and building systems intended to reduce harm rather than only react to it. VRChat distinguished this conduct-focused work from content tools such as [[Content Gating]], which can hide an avatar or world but cannot address how people behave. VRChat said it planned a dedicated post in July 2026 covering how the system works, how it was designed, and how the experiment would run, including how users could take part.<ref name="SafetyUpdate2026" />

On {{Date|2026-07-30}}, Tupper said the system had been delayed after effort shifted to related priorities on the Trust & Safety team's internal roadmap, with no current ETA. He said the community would still be informed well in advance of testing.<ref name="TupperPublicInstance2026-07-30">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-30-july-2026/48750/17 Reply] by Tupper on ''ask.vrchat.com''; posted July 30, 2026; retrieved August 13, 2026.</ref>

=== OSC: Output for Haptics ===

A milestone created in 2022 on the VRChat Community OSC GitHub repository proposes streaming OSC data representing touches or collisions with avatars to interface with haptic devices.<ref name="osc-milestones">[https://github.com/vrchat-community/osc/milestones Milestones] on ''github.com/vrchat-community/osc''; retrieved April 6, 2026.</ref>

=== OSC: Udon ===

A milestone created in 2022 on the VRChat Community OSC GitHub repository plans to enable [[Udon]] to read and write OSC data for use in VRChat worlds.<ref name="osc-milestones" />

=== Render pipeline migration (URP) ===

Community discussion periodically suggests migrating VRChat from Unity's Built-in Render Pipeline (BiRP) to URP or HDRP. No official release announcement or Open Beta plan has been published for a migration of this scope.

In a Unity forum thread on render pipeline strategy, a Unity staff member said Unity hoped to share more details during the year on "how we are migrating one of the largest UGC platforms to URP".<ref name="UnityURP2026">[https://discussions.unity.com/t/render-pipelines-strategy-for-2026/1710004/206 Post] on ''discussions.unity.com''; posted February 27, 2026; retrieved June 25, 2026.</ref> The platform was not named, but was a reply to questions about VRChat.

=== Image paste into inventory media ===

A {{Date|2026-07-16}} Developer Update described a forthcoming way to paste JPG, PNG, or clipboard images into VRChat as [[Prints]], [[Inventory#User Icons|user icons]], [[Stickers]], and [[Emojis]]. An image can be pasted as raw data, pasted as a file, or dragged and dropped. Stickers, user icons, and emojis are padded to a square with transparency by default; Prints keep their original shape. Portrait Prints are rotated automatically, with a separate control for further rotation. When the clipboard already holds image data, a Paste icon appears on the Quick Menu launch pad and does the same thing as Ctrl+V.<ref name="DU2026-07-16">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-16-july-2026/48702 "Developer Update - 16 July 2026"] on ''ask.vrchat.com''; dated July 16, 2026; retrieved August 13, 2026.</ref>

=== Group Nameplate Banner ===

Group management on the website is planned to gain a Group Nameplate Banner, a separate image from the existing group banner and used only on the group's nameplate. Groups that do not upload one keep using the existing banner. The upload flow includes a template.

Two crop modes were described. Bottom-left Anchored pins the image's bottom-left corner so that a longer nameplate reveals more of the image without changing its scale. Centered scales the image to cover the banner, keeping a marked center square always visible while the rest can crop as the nameplate grows or shrinks.<ref name="DU2026-07-30">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-30-july-2026/48750 "Developer Update - 30 July 2026"] on ''ask.vrchat.com''; dated July 30, 2026; retrieved August 13, 2026.</ref>

=== Custom nameplate banners without a group ===

VRChat also planned custom nameplate banners that can be uploaded individually, including by users who are not in a [[Groups|group]]. That change is scheduled to follow shortly after the 2026.3.1 launch rather than ship on day one.<ref name="DU2026-07-30" />

=== Udon update ===

An upcoming [[Udon]] update is planned to add native APIs so world objects can face the local player or follow a humanoid avatar bone without per-frame update loops, which VRChat described as expensive. Both APIs are subject to change until release.<ref name="DU2026-08-13">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-13-august-2026/48800 "Developer Update - 13 August 2026"] on ''ask.vrchat.com''; dated August 13, 2026; retrieved August 13, 2026.</ref>

Native billboarding registers a transform with <code>VRCBillboard.Register</code> and removes it with <code>VRCBillboard.Unregister</code>. The default register call tracks yaw only; an overload with <code>allowTilt</code> also tracks pitch.

Attaching a transform to a bone currently requires moving and rotating the object every frame. Native <code>AttachTransformToBone</code> and <code>DetachTransformFromBone</code> methods are planned so that tracking is handled after a one-time attach.

The August 2026 Creators Roadmap lists this work as in progress.<ref name="Roadmap2026-08">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/vrchat-creators-roadmap-august-2026/48896 "VRChat Creators Roadmap (August 2026)"] on ''ask.vrchat.com''; dated August 31, 2026; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref>

=== Advanced contact proximity parameters ===

When a [[Avatar Dynamics#Contacts|contact]] receiver is hit by a sender with at least one matching tag, it can already generate a proximity parameter that indicates how close the sender is. An upcoming SDK update is planned to add further parameters.

The extra parameters include the sender type, the local midpoint of the sender relative to the receiver, velocity and speed, the rate at which proximity is changing, and up to 16 boolean parameters for tags the sender shares with the receiver. If several senders contact the same receiver, the values represent the sender with the highest proximity. VRChat said the additions follow community feedback and are intended to replace workarounds used to derive the same information.<ref name="DU2026-08-13" />

=== Material Contacts ===

Material Contacts writes contact transforms into shader properties. When it is enabled on a receiver, the receiver can target up to four <code>MeshRenderer</code> components. Those renderers receive the world-space transform matrix of the receiver's four nearest contacting senders, and of the receiver itself.<ref name="DU2026-08-27">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-27-august-2026/48877 "Developer Update - 27 August 2026"] on ''ask.vrchat.com''; dated August 27, 2026; retrieved August 27, 2026.</ref>

Contacts currently update at most 60 times per second. That cap is being removed, so contacts can update every frame above 60 FPS.<ref name="DU2026-08-27" />

=== Variable-width avatar parameters ===

Synced avatar parameters use three types. Integers are 8-bit values from 0 to 255. Floats are 8-bit fixed-point values from −1.0 to 1.0. Booleans are 1-bit true or false.<ref name="DU2026-08-27" />

Integer and float parameters will use a configurable number of bits. A lower bit width frees unused space in the 256-bit synced-parameter budget. A higher bit width allows integers above 255, or more float precision, and uses more of that budget. A 2-bit integer can replace several mutually exclusive boolean toggles. One example uses a 2-bit Outfit parameter (0 to 3) and a 4-bit EyeConstriction float. That setup uses 7 bits instead of 17. The inspector is subject to change.<ref name="DU2026-08-27" />

=== Soba ===

[[Soba]] remains in development toward a Closed Beta. VRChat described the language itself as "in good shape." The largest implemented change relative to [[Udon]] is non-behavior classes: plain classes that do not inherit from a behavior, whereas in Udon every piece of code must live on an UdonBehaviour. Also implemented are structs, interfaces, custom interfaces, static variables, nested types, and exception logs with a full stack trace of user code.

Remaining work includes confirming that implemented behavior works in a real client, plus test coverage, editor tooling, validation, error messages, and documentation. VRChat did not give a Closed Beta date, saying it would rather under-promise after a March 2026 update that described the team as "hard at work" and then stretched five more months. Soba is designed to sit alongside Udon, not replace it.<ref name="DU2026-08-13" />

=== Portal exclusion zones ===

World creators currently choose to disable [[Portals]] completely, or to allow them anywhere except the player spawn area. Work in progress adds exclusion zones, which are areas where players cannot place portals.<ref name="CannyPortalDropZones">[https://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/world-request-designating-portal-drop-zones "World request: designating portal drop zones"] on ''feedback.vrchat.com''; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref> The change is intended for games and other spaces where players should not walk into a dropped portal. More details are planned for an upcoming Developer Update.<ref name="Roadmap2026-08" />

=== Avatar optimizer ===

An official avatar optimizer was removed from the August 2026 Creators Roadmap for now. It is expected to return.<ref name="CannyAvatarOptimizer">[https://feedback.vrchat.com/avatar-30/p/automatic-avatar-optimization-in-sdk "Automatic Avatar Optimization in SDK"] on ''feedback.vrchat.com''; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref> [[#Unity 6|Unity 6]] support is prioritized first because it affects the optimizer's features and functionality. The optimizer is also intended to work with popular third-party avatar optimizers. Optimization is intended to be easier without many new ways to break an avatar on upload.<ref name="Roadmap2026-08" />

