=== Discovery and social system improvements ===

[[File:For-You-Discovery-Page.jpg|thumb|Earlier "For You" world list experiment]]
[[File:Discover-Alpha-Live-Tab.jpg|thumb|Discover (Alpha) on the Live tab of the Main Menu]]
VRChat stated it is exploring improvements to discovery and social systems so users can find intended communities while naturally separating audiences that should not interact.<ref name="TrustSafety2025Blog" /> No specific features or timeline were announced.

In a developer stream Q&A on {{Date|May 29, 2026}}, the team described a personalized "For You" world list as an experiment that was running at the time, noting that users may see it, see variations of it, or not see it at all, and that no further details would be shared while the experiment was in progress.<ref name="ForYouWorldList">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/may-29-developer-stream-q-a-summary/48500 "May 29 Developer Stream Q&A Summary"] on ''ask.vrchat.com''; posted June 1, 2026; retrieved June 9, 2026.</ref>

As of {{Date|July 2026}}, the "For You" world list was no longer observed in the client.

An A/B test labeled Discover (Alpha) has been observed on the Live tab of the Main Menu. First observed {{Date|2026-07-24}}.

=== Unity 6 ===

Engine upgrade to Unity 6 (6000.0.67f1) is available on PC on the <code>unity-6</code> branch.<ref name="DiscordUnity6">[https://discord.com/channels/189511567539306508/503009489486872583 #open-beta-announcements] on VRChat Discord; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref> The branch opened at 6000.0.60f1.<ref name="DU2026-06-25">[https://ask.vrchat.com/t/developer-update-25-june-2026/48618 "Developer Update - 25 June 2026"] on ''ask.vrchat.com''; dated June 25, 2026; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref> Bugs can be reported in the [https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta Open Beta] canny board.

Unity 6 SDK and [[VRChat Creator Companion|VCC]] support is in QA as of {{Date|2026-08-27}}. The later Unity 6 SDK and VCC open beta installs Unity 6 through VCC and migrates projects.<ref name="DU2026-08-27" />

=== Action Drivers ===

Action Drivers is an upcoming avatar [[VRChat SDK|SDK]] component in closed beta testing. It is subject to change.<ref name="DU2026-08-27" />

Creators bind avatar parameters to actions such as toggling GameObjects or changing blend shapes. Action Drivers does not replace custom animators.<ref name="DU2026-08-27" /> Material swaps are being handled as part of Action Drivers.<ref name="CannyMaterialSwap">[https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/material-swap-dedicated-componentbehavior "Material Swap: Dedicated Component/Behavior"] on ''feedback.vrchat.com''; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref>

=== World analytics ===

World analytics is in progress at a very early stage.<ref name="CannyWorldAnalytics">[https://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/give-world-creators-access-to-analytics-about-their-world "Give world creators access to analytics about their world"] on ''feedback.vrchat.com''; retrieved August 31, 2026.</ref> A small test gives additional, rudimentary analytics to a few dozen invited world creators. That group is as many as can be supported without a full system. The test is intended to learn which analytics matter and how creators use them. Work next year is planned to use those findings to build a system that supports many more creators. Building that system is expected to take quite a bit of time.<ref name="Roadmap2026-08" />

